          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.064,
            0.835,
            0.082
          ],
          "content": "Lines and Angles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.12,
            0.834,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": "360 equal angles or parts. The angle measure of each of these unit parts is 1 degree, which is written as 1°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.166,
            0.834,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "This unit part is used to assign measure to any angle: the measure of an angle is the number of $1 ^ { \\circ }$ unit parts it contains inside it. For example, see this figure:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.324,
            0.231,
            0.653,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.37,
            0.835,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "It contains 30 units of 1° angle and so we say that its angle measure is $3 0 ^ { \\circ }$ **Measures of different angles:** What is the measure of a full turn in degrees? As we have taken it to contain 360 degrees, its measure is $3 6 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.452,
            0.835,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": "What is the measure of a straight angle in degrees? A straight angle is half of a full turn. As a full-turn is $3 6 0 ^ { \\circ } ]$ , a half turn is $1 8 0 ^ { \\circ }$ What is the measure of a right angle in degrees? Two right angles together form a straight angle. As a straight angle measures $1 8 0 ^ { \\circ } ,$ , a right angle measures 90°."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.233,
            0.572,
            0.436,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
